 "origin": "Built by Muse (AI assistant) on 18 November 2026 at Steven Powell's request for a physics room, 'Everyday Physics' \u2014 the last of the science trio he named (after Everyday Chemistry and Everyday Electronics): a playable pool table with the physics drawn on (ghost aim line, cushion reflection with incoming and outgoing angles measured from the cushion's face and labelled equal, equal-mass elastic collisions that exchange the velocity components along the line of centres so momentum visibly hands over, speed arrows, pause/step, simple potting with stated simplifications), a ballistics launcher in the Angry Birds style on an honest scale (60 m range, real metres and seconds, g = 9.8, no air resistance \u2014 stated on the page; dotted trajectories kept for comparison, a crate target at 45 m, and a same-speed three-angles compare), a pendulum bench (period from string length only) and a seesaw bench (weight x distance), four kitchen-table experiment cards (balloon rocket, egg drop, paper airplane lab, pendulum painting), a verified links shelf (PhET Projectile Motion, PhET Collision Lab, The Physics Classroom, Khan Academy Physics) plus the 'Read deeper \u2014 Wikipedia' group Steven asked for on the Electronics pattern (Physics, Classical mechanics, Projectile motion, Momentum), a plain-language workshop on reflection/momentum/parabolas/the pendulum/torque, and a Help menu with full documentation. No upstream original exists; the collection copy is the maintained original.",
